%I A398645 #16 Sep 17 2026 23:58:31
%S A398645 1,1,0,1,1,3,7,24,116,1179,22824,941428,76728688,11921081036
%N A398645 Number of unlabeled Eulerian point-determining graphs on n vertices.
%C A398645 A graph is Eulerian if every vertex has even degree. A graph is point-determining (or mating) if distinct vertices have distinct open neighborhoods.
%H A398645 I. M. Gessel and J. Li, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcta.2010.03.009">Enumeration of point-determining graphs</a>, J. Combinatorial Theory Ser. A 118 (2011), 591-612.
%F A398645 By Burnside's lemma, a(n) = Sum_{lambda partition of n} Fix(lambda)/z_lambda, where z_lambda = Product_i i^m_i*m_i!, m_i is the multiplicity of i in lambda, and Fix(lambda) is the number of labeled Eulerian point-determining graphs fixed by a permutation of cycle type lambda.
%F A398645 Fix(lambda) = Sum_{rho in Pi_n^sigma} mu_sigma(rho)*2^d(sigma,rho), where sigma is any permutation in S_n of cycle type lambda, Pi_n^sigma is the lattice of sigma-invariant set partitions of [n], mu_sigma is its Möbius function from the discrete partition, and d(sigma,rho) is the dimension over GF(2) of the space of sigma-invariant graphs that are Eulerian and have equal open neighborhoods within every block of rho.
%e A398645 For n=6, writing ij for the edge {i,j}, the 7 graphs can be represented on vertex set {1,...,6} by the edge sets {12,13,14,15,25,34}, {14,15,23,25,34}, {15,16,24,26,34,35}, {12,13,15,16,23,24,26,34,35}, {12,13,14,15,23,24,25,34,35,45}, {12,16,26,34,35,45}, {12,13,14,16,23,24,26,34,35,45}. Hence a(6)=7.
%Y A398645 Cf. A399730 (labeled Eulerian point-determining graphs), A004110 (unlabeled point-determining graphs), A006024 (labeled point-determining graphs).
%K A398645 nonn,more,new
%O A398645 0,6
%A A398645 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 16 2026
